From 42f59f1864a77ae660ae2dfb987cb3d4c713536f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:13:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] [iOS] Pick Gemma's file, backend, and precision per
 session

Sessions that read only text run the text-only GPU file
(gemma-4-E2B-it-gpu.litertlm) on the GPU from Apple GPU family 6 (A13)
on, unless the multimodal file is already there and the GPU runs it.
Sessions whose expectedInputs include images or audio run the
multimodal file (gemma-4-E2B-it.litertlm), on the GPU from family 7
(A14) on and on the CPU before that. Families 5 and older use the CPU,
untested on the GPU. Each file downloads when a session first needs
it, and one engine is loaded at a time.

On an iPhone 11 Pro Max (A13, 4 GB): text on the GPU file at 22 tokens
per second, 0.4 GB of footprint; an image session on the multimodal
file on the CPU at 14 tokens per second, describing the image
correctly. The multimodal file on the A13 GPU produces random tokens.
On family 7, where 16-bit activations corrupt digits (LiteRT-LM issues
2814 and 3913), the multimodal file runs with 32-bit activations.

Text-only files get no encoders configured, which made their
conversations fail to start.
